### Env / secrets ###
# This repository needs CDE_JWT_SECRET and CDE_STORAGE_SIGNING_KEY to start,
# and the natural place to keep them is a .env that docker compose reads. That
# file must never be committable: the JWT key signs the tenant claim, so
# publishing it lets anyone mint a token for any tenant (§5.6). The frontend
# repo already ignored .env; this one did not, which is the more dangerous of
# the two to miss.
#
# .env.example is the exception — a committed template with placeholder names
# and no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

